 "version": 1,
 "_comment": "DATA-DRIVEN concept->icon map (WO concept-icon). A conceptId (abilityId / skillId / effect / itemId / owner concept token, lower-cased) maps to a real sprite addressed by { role, name, override? } in RpgUiCatalog (role 'icons' = Resources/RpgUi/icons/*, role 'potion' = Resources/RpgUi/potion/*, etc.). ConceptIconResolver loads this once and returns RpgUiCatalog.Get(role,name); a missing art file yields null so the caller keeps its glyph/class-art fallback. OPTIONAL per-entry boolean 'override' (default false/absent): when true the concept FORCES its Obsidian icon over a caller's own richer art (the defaults bar uses ResolveAnyOverride -> class art -> ResolveAny gap-fill). Leave override absent to keep today's behavior (class art wins on the defaults bar). This file is the SINGLE source of the mapping \u2014 no icon choices live in C#. Edit here to re-skin/override any concept. Real icons present today: icon_combat, icon_sword, icon_shield, icon_heart, icon_inventory, icon_quest, icon_compass, icon_talk, icon_tree, icon_settings.",
